Now assign a number $f(i)$ to each state. It may be energy, momentum, or any other quantity we wish to measure. Its expectation value is $\langle f\rangle=\sum_i f(i)p_i.$ Bracket notation is convenient even outside quantum mechanics. In frequency language the same average is $\langle f\rangle
 =
 \lim_{N_{\mathrm{trials}}\to\infty}
 \frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{trials}}}
 \sum_i f(i)N(i).$

