p.src:
Entropy is additive for uncorrelated systems. If $p_{ij}=p_i^{(A)}p_j^{(B)},$ then $\begin{aligned}S_{AB}
 &=-\sum_{i,j}p_i^{(A)}p_j^{(B)}
 \log\!\left[p_i^{(A)}p_j^{(B)}\right]\\
 &=S_A+S_B.
 \end{aligned}$ Correlations prevent this factorization and reduce the independent uncertainty of the pair.

